Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 11/15/2024]
1. Resonance energies are adopted from Gade et al. 2008, Sun et al. 2019, Longfellow et al. 2019. For higher-lying resonances, expected above 2 MeV resonance 
   energy, the experimental Ex values in the 27Mg mirror nucleus are not consistent with the results for 27P reported in the elastic scattering experiment of Jung 
   et al. 2012 or the Coulomb dissociation experiment of Marganiec et al. 2016.
2. The proton widths and the direct capture S factor are calculated using the experimental spectroscopic factors of the 27Mg mirror levels, given in Endt 1977 
   and D'Agata et al. 2021.
3. The gamma-ray partial widths are estimated from the experimental lifetimes of the 27Mg mirror states (ENSDF 2010); except for Er = 319 keV: our adopted value
   is equal to the geometric mean of the independent theoretical values presented by Herndl et al. 1995, Caggiano et al. 2011, Togano et al. 2011, Marganiec et al.
   2016, and the value deduced from the measured lifetime of the 27Mg mirror state.

